d":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\nv4.4.dev6.official [1f47e4c4e]\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Fedora Linux 41 (Workstation Edition) - Wayland - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7800 XT (RADV NAVI32) - AMD Ryzen 9 3900X 12-Core Processor (24 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm writing a GUI app using Godot. When I run the app on Android, I have to call `set_content_scale_factor` on the main window in order to not have the GUI elements look microscopic (in this case, the scale factor is 3.0). The text of UI items in the main window and the titles of sub-windows look great but the UI text of items in the sub-windows looks terrible.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7686d193-1046-48cb-a827-7f493f6bf1f6)\n\nI can use multi-channel SDF, which gives better results, but the text is still rendered at a lower resolution and scaled up for sub-windows, so it looks blurry.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/16a7408f-cd8f-48bb-871b-4e4873bad9ed)\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee description above.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nProject is available [here](https://github.com/Barugon/aviate).","closed_by":{"login":"Barugon","id":16503728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTAzNzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16503728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Barugon","html_url":"https://github.com/Barugon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Barugon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Barugon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Barugon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Barugon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Barugon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/user